{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"A material harness flaw (my pump omitted the app's persist duty) taints that receipt; I must record it before the claim rests on it."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Correct the third question's account after diagnosing a material harness fault in its retained receipt: the probe's message pump consumed the wrapped node's Readys and called Advance but never wrote Ready.Entries or Ready.HardState to that node's storage, so the application duty 'write HardState, Entries and Snapshot to persistent storage before the messages are sent' (doc.go:75-78, and the Ready contract in node.go:58-80) was omitted. Two observations follow from the omission and are now recorded: raft moved those entries out of its unstable log on Advance so the node's last entry identity read as (0,0) although its commit index was 4, and the later campaign lost because the vote request advertised that empty log. The witness itself (Propose blocked after the re-add) is not explained by this omission, but the receipt's prefix is not a conforming application prefix, so the execution-backed claim is downgraded to conditional until a corrected harness re-measures it; the corrective action is identified in the limitations.\\\",\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"7f6aa45d046c4714992282dd5e6d8389-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"node-propc-guard\\\",\\\"node-propc-restore\\\",\\\"node-propose-block\\\",\\\"node-propose-doc\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"8b3e88d4b4a641fa8ddc723ecc0ba56d\\\":[1,2,3,4]},\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"conditional\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Source side the account is unchanged and independent of the harness fault: node.run sets its proposal channel to nil when an applied configuration change removes the local node from Progress and the node is in neither cs.Voters nor cs.VotersOutgoing (node.go:400-432), it restores the channel from n.propc only in the branch that reacts to a change of r.lead with a leader known (node.go:343-380), and Node.Propose sends into that channel, so a nil channel makes the call wait for the caller's context or the node's done channel (node.go:514-551); the target's own comment calls this reset 'not very sound and likely has bugs' (node.go:409-411) and the only documented caveat is that proposals can be lost without notice (node.go:138-140). Execution side, receipt 8b3e88d4b4a641fa8ddc723ecc0ba56d still shows the control holding (parsed index 1: while node 2 is a plain member that knows leader 1, Propose returns no error in 0ms and the leader's log index advances to 2) and the witness violated (parsed index 4: after the removal and the re-add were applied, with the leader's configuration back to voters=(1 2), node 2 committed and applied 4 and still knowing leader 1 in term 1, Propose returns only when its 300ms deadline fires and the leader's log index stays at 4), and the four remaining comparisons are unknown only because the compared fields sit inside the events' node2_state object. What this update corrects is the applicability of that receipt: the probe's pump called the wrapper's Ready/Advance loop but omitted the application's persistence duty - it never wrote Ready.Entries or Ready.HardState to the wrapped node's storage, although the contract requires HardState, Entries and Snapshot to be on stable storage before the messages of the same Ready are sent (doc.go:75-78, node.go:58-80) - so the prefix is not one a conforming application produces. The fault is visible in the draft harness: node 2's last entry identity reads (0,0) while its commit index is 4, because Advance removes entries from the unstable log under the assumption that the application has written them, and the same fault is why the attempted leadership-change control lost its election (the vote request advertised the empty log and the leader rejected it). The witness's mechanism is not explained by the fault - propc is set only by the two branches in run(), and the removal branch depends solely on the applied configuration change - but a claim that rests on a retained receipt needs a conforming prefix, so the account is stated as conditional on that correction rather than as an established comparison, and the corrective action is recorded.\\\",\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n   \\\"The retained receipt's prefix omits the application's persistence duty, so it is not yet evidence that a conforming application reaches this state; the receipt's witness comparison cannot be relied on as a completed applicable comparison until a corrected harness is executed.\\\",\n   \\\"The control comparison still holds in the same receipt (an error-free proposal before the removal), which shows the blocked behaviour is specific to the state after the removal and the re-add rather than a property of the harness in general.\\\",\n   \\\"The Node.Propose documentation warns that proposals can be lost without notice (node.go:138-140), so a caller with a deadline and retries is not blocked; the claim under test is that the channel stays closed while the node is a member again and a leader is known.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"The corrective action for the harness is identified: on every Ready the pump must write Ready.Entries to the wrapped node's storage, apply Ready.Snapshot when present, persist a non-empty Ready.HardState, and only then send the Ready's messages and call Advance; after that, the same control, premise and witness observations must be re-measured, and the state fields that the unknown comparisons read must be emitted at the event top level.\\\",\n   \\\"The harness drives a wrapped node against a bare raft instance, so the wrapper's asynchronous ready/advance contract is exercised on one side only, and both nodes run in one process.\\\",\n   \\\"The proposed call uses a 300ms deadline; the receipt measures that the call did not complete within it and that the group's log did not change, not how long the channel stays closed in absolute terms.\\\",\n   \\\"The leadership-change restore path remains unmeasured; the failed attempt is now explained by the harness fault and must be retried on the corrected harness.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"The proposal channel is closed by the removal guard and restored only by a leadership change with a leader known.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-knowledge-1\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"With a nil proposal channel Propose blocks until the caller's context or the node's done channel fires.\\\"}\n  ]}]}\nopen('update18.json','w').write(json.dumps(u,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run --submission update18.json 2>&1 | tail -4\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
