osed call uses a 300ms deadline; the receipt measures that the call did not complete within it and that the group's log did not change, not how long the channel stays closed in absolute terms.\\\",\n   \\\"The leadership-change restore path remains unmeasured; the failed attempt is now explained by the harness fault and must be retried on the corrected harness.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"The proposal channel is closed by the removal guard and restored only by a leadership change with a leader known.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-knowledge-1\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"With a nil proposal channel Propose blocks until the caller's context or the node's done channel fires.\\\"}\n  ]}]}\nopen('update18.json','w').write(json.dumps(u,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run --submission update18.json 2>&1 | tail -4\"","aggregated_output":"{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"10b3ddfa3d914121bb0b6c1901d393f6\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 2496.397289383007, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\", \"no_change\": false, \"execution_requested\": false, \"effects\": [{\"object\": \"interpretations\", \"action\": \"append\", \"target\": \"interpretations[0]\", \"investigation_id\": \"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-question-0\", \"changed_fields\": [\"conclusion\", \"rationale\", \"counterevidence\", \"limitations\"]}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update18.json\",\"summary\":\"Corrected the third question's account after diagnosing a material fault in my own harness. The probe's pump consumed the wrapped node's Readys and called Advance but never wrote Ready.Entries or Ready.HardState to that node's storage, so the retained receipt 8b3e88d4b4a641fa8ddc723ecc0ba56d rests on a prefix that omits the application duty 'write HardState, Entries and Snapshot to stable storage before the messages are sent' (doc.go:75-78, node.go:58-80); the fault is visible in the harness as a node whose last entry identity reads (0,0) while its commit index is 4, and it also explains why the attempted leadership-change control lost its election (the vote request advertised that empty log and was rejected). The execution-backed claim is therefore downgraded from violated to conditional on a corrected prefix, while the source account stays unchanged and independent of the fault: the channel is closed by the removal guard (node.go:400-432) and restored only by a leadership change with a leader known (node.go:343-380), and Propose on a nil channel waits for the caller's context or the node's done channel (node.go:514-551), with the target's own comment calling the mechanism unsound. The receipt's control still holds (index 1) and the witness is still violated (index 4), and the four unknown comparisons are explained as field nesting rather than missing observations; the witness's mechanism is not explained by the fault, but a claim resting on a retained receipt needs a conforming prefix. The corrective action is recorded in the limitations: persist each Ready's entries, snapshot and hard state before sending its messages and advancing, emit the compared state fields at the event top level, and re-measure the control, the premises, the witness and the leadership-change restore path on that corrected harness. No new execution was requested this turn.\"}"}}
